    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1332">

                <pb facs="1082" n="1072" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1072"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/3–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubby</hi>)<anchor n="45" xml:id="d1332-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-21T15:00:00-05:00">March 21, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. Urtel unnumbered [<hi rendition="#italic">129</hi>] March 6 economic
                    conditions since Jan. 15.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d1332-f2"/> For action Tientsin
                    Shanghai, would ConGen consider feasible attempt send courier commercial vessels
                    Shanghai–Taku Bar under present conditions. Is pouch exchange Taku Bar or
                    alternate procedure possible. Dept anxious reestablish direct communications.
                    Your opinion requested necessity sending two couriers for security.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1332-f1" n="45" type="source" xml:id="d1332-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Consul General at Tientsin as telegram No. 60.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1332-f2" n="46" xml:id="d1332-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
